parsed_suggested_fix:
Split the class by responsibility: extract an InvoiceTotalCalculator, IAmountFormatter, IContactResolver, and a stateless StatementBuilder that orchestrates them. Pass statement sections as local variables and make summary generation depend on explicit input rather than prior method calls. Remove caching unless profiling proves it useful; if retained, keep separate caches per formatting operation and define culture explicitly. Validate or encode account IDs before incorporating them into addresses.

Example:
public sealed class StatementBuilder
{
    private readonly IInvoiceTotalCalculator _totals;
    private readonly IAmountFormatter _amounts;
    private readonly IContactResolver _contacts;

    public StatementBuilder(IInvoiceTotalCalculator totals,
        IAmountFormatter amounts, IContactResolver contacts)
    {
        _totals = totals;
        _amounts = amounts;
        _contacts = contacts;
    }

    public string Build(Account account, IEnumerable<Invoice> invoices)
    {
        var sections = new List<string>
        {
            string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(account.Name)
                ? "UNKNOWN ACCOUNT"
                : $"STATEMENT FOR {account.Name}",
            $"contact: {_contacts.Resolve(account)}"
        };

        var total = _totals.Calculate(invoices);
        sections.Add($"TOTAL {_amounts.Format(total)}");
        return string.Join(Environment.NewLine, sections);
    }
}

Give each extracted component focused unit tests, including boundary values, invalid IDs, culture behavior, and concurrent use of the orchestrator.
